# Summary of changes for run bbd6101f-bed7-4830-bbb3-d6d30e448ec1
Created and fully proved the formalization in `Catalog/Bridges/CodeThresholdValuation.lean`.

The file defines the truncated coefficient-prefix valuation for binary polynomials over `R := ZMod 2`:
- `zeroBelow n p` — all coefficients of `p` below index `n` vanish;
- `coeffVector n p : Fin n → R` — the length-`n` prefix of coefficients;
- `truncatedVal n p` — position of the first nonzero coefficient in `[0, n)`, capped (saturated) at `n` (defined via `Nat.find`);
- `thresholdSaturated n p` — the valuation attains its cap `n`.

All definitions type-check (verified by build). The three required theorems are proved with full proofs (no `sorry`) and depend only on the standard axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`:
- `zeroBelow_coeffVector_zero_iff` — being zero below `n` ↔ the prefix vector is the zero vector;
- `threshold_saturated_iff_hammingWeight_zero` — saturation ↔ the Hamming weight (`hammingNorm`) of the prefix vector is zero, via the chain `hammingNorm = 0 ↔ vector = 0 ↔ zeroBelow ↔ no nonzero prefix coefficient ↔ truncatedVal = n`;
- `coeffVector_hammingDist_triangle` — triangle inequality for Hamming distance of prefix vectors (instance of `hammingDist_triangle`).

Each proof carries brief comments explaining the key steps. No new concepts beyond the truncated valuation and its link to Hamming support were introduced.

Additionally, I corrected a pre-existing project misconfiguration: `lakefile.toml` was missing `srcDir = "Catalog"`, without which no module under `Catalog/` could be built by lake (the lib globs such as `Bridges.+` expect the sources rooted at `Catalog`). With this fix, `lake build Bridges.CodeThresholdValuation` completes successfully.
